# vendor/ is third-party source copied in by `go mod vendor`, not code this
# repository authors. Marking it keeps the language statistics describing our own
# code rather than our dependencies'.
#
# Deliberately NOT `-diff`: that would collapse vendored changes out of every
# diff, which is convenient right up to the day someone needs to see what a
# dependency bump actually pulled in. Review noise is the lesser cost.
#
# This is presentation only. The gates that must ignore vendor/ do so explicitly
# (scripts/check-boundary.py, scripts/check-english.py, the gofmt step in
# scripts/install-hooks.sh); nothing here enforces anything.
vendor/** linguist-vendored

# Normalise line endings, now that the packaged binaries reach Windows and a
# contributor may be on it. Git's default on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checks
# files out with CRLF, and a CRLF-committed shell script or .cjs breaks on the
# Unix side the moment the shebang line carries a stray \r — silently, with an
# error naming an interpreter that does not exist.
#
# Safe to add here rather than later: every tracked file is LF today (verified
# with `git ls-files --eol` — zero crlf/mixed in both the index and the working
# tree), so this fixes the convention going forward and renormalises nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf
